<title>GERMANY: Kirch says talks on Premiere not tied to Italy.</title>
<headline>Kirch says talks on Premiere not tied to Italy.</headline>
<dateline>MUNICH, Germany 1997-06-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Kirch Group is holding talks with France's Canal-Plus about the German and the Italian pay-TV markets, but there is no tie between the two issues, a Kirch spokesman said on Monday.</p>
<p>Kirch and Bertelsmann affiliate CLT-UFA announced they plan to operate German pay-TV broadcaster Premiere as a 50-50 venture.</p>
<p>Canal-Plus, which now holds 37.5 percent of Premiere, was said in the joint statement to be satisfied with the deal, but declined to comment itself.</p>
<p>Canal-Plus is reportedly interested in acquiring Kirch's 45 percent stake in Italy's Telepiu in exchange for withdrawing from Premiere, but the Kirch spokesman said the two issues were not linked.</p>
<p>Kirch now owns 25 percent of Premiere, while CLT-UFA owns 37.5 percent.</p>
<p>-- Terence Gallagher, Bonn newsroom, 49-228-2609750</p>
